	"VersionNumber": 1,
	"ResourceName": "okta_user_aggregates",
	"Description": "Okta user-directory aggregates, rebuilt every hour by the scheduled search \"Okta - User Aggregates\" (table -save -update rowkey). Do not edit; the next run overwrites matching rows.\n\nColumns: ts,metric,key,value,rowkey. ts is the run time in Unix seconds.\nSnapshot metrics (rowkey metric|key): status, user_type, division, department, title, manager, timezone, provider_type, provider_name, last_signin, password_age, avg_password_age_days, avg_days_created_to_activated. A key that no longer occurs keeps its last count.\nHistory metrics (rowkey ts|metric|key, one point per run, never pruned): last_signin_history, password_age_history.\n\nRead a snapshot with: dump -r okta_user_aggregates metric==\"status\" key value\nRead a trend with:    dump -r okta_user_aggregates -t ts metric==\"last_signin_history\" ts key value\nShips with only the header row; the scheduled search fills it on its first run.",
